        {
          "question": "e-3127",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "To find $\\dfrac {\\partial^2 f }{\\partial x\\partial y},$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\\dfrac {\\partial f}{\\partial y}$ with respect to $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\u2202}^{2}f}{\u2202x\u2202y} & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\frac{2y}{x+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =2y\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}({(x+{y}^{2})}^{-1}) \\\\  & =-2y(x+{y}^{2})^{-2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2y}{{(x+{y}^{2})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
